\ An AOT binary runs the dictionary-shadow guard at the default severity. A source file cannot set
\ the relaxing pragma and a binary reads no startup file, so no set site is reachable and the guard
\ has nothing to read. The .env names a startup file relaxing both keys, and the throw below is what
\ shows that relaxation never arrives.
\
\ The collision has to happen at binary runtime, not at freeze. The freeze executes the entry file's
\ statements ending in `;` and collects the rest. The trailing `0 drop` keeps this definition
\ for binary runtime in the durable entry frame, where the guard reads.
\
\ The call is bare rather than wrapped in `recover`, because a quotation pushes a transient frame
\ and a definition landing there is exempt by design. A word body pushes one of its own the same
\ way, so a definition made inside a called word never reaches the guard either. So the binary
\ aborts, and its diagnostic is the golden.
\
\ The import is not load-bearing for the frame: every AOT binary pushes the durable entry frame at
\ boot. The import stays so this entry covers the guard with an imported name sitting in the frame.
use { taken: } "fixtures/aot_collision_guard_mod.1z" ;

taken .

dup: ( -- x ) [ 0 ] ; 0 drop
